---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
import ProjectTags from "../../components/ProjectTags.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout>
  <article class="space-y-12">
    <header class="space-y-5">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold">Cookbook</h1>
      <p class="max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700">
        A personal cooking library for saving recipes, organizing them around how they are used, and making them practical at mealtime.
      </p>
      <ProjectTags />
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">The Idea</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-700">
        Recipes are easier to use when the collection reflects real cooking decisions. The library combines dish role, cuisine, cooking technique, saved collections, and practical details such as prep time, cook time, and adjustable servings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Design Priorities</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-gray-700">
        <li>Keep recipe browsing calm, legible, and comfortable on a phone.</li>
        <li>Use structured categories and saved filters instead of uncontrolled tags.</li>
        <li>Make ingredient and direction views quick to scan while cooking.</li>
        <li>Keep private recipes and service credentials out of public source and portfolio media.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="border-t border-gray-200 pt-6 text-sm text-gray-500">
      The source and live cookbook are private. A short interface demo can be added after preparing a review-safe sample collection.
    </p>
  </article>
</ProjectLayout>
